            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0146" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-19T18:00:00+01:00">October 19, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 19—2:46 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3297. Depcirtel October 12, 11 a. m. Secretary General Foreign Office has assured
                    me Italian Government (reference 1335, May 6) does not propose independent
                    action re recognition Chinese Communist regime without prior consultation US. He
                    would appreciate having as soon as possible any further views that we may have
                    in that regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
